{"items":[{"tags":["react-native","expo"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":62953380,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1767303331,"creation_date":1594986708,"body":"I&#39;m still new to expo. I try to resolve this problem but I found a dead road could someone help me?\nI try to connect  to , so when someone presses the button of the flatlist in , it will go to .\nI currently get an:\n\nError while reading multipart response\n\non my phone.\n\nThis is my  file\n\nThis is my  file\n\n","excerpt":"props);\n        //setting default state\n        this.state = { isLoading: true, search: &#39;&#39; };\n        this.arrayholder = [];\n    }\n    componentDidMount() {\n        return fetch(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"error &quot; Unable to resolve &quot;./component/Search&quot; from &quot;components\\Description.js&quot;"},{"tags":["javascript","android","ios","reactjs","react-native"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":62594549,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1765663226,"creation_date":1593173764,"body":"I am new to React-Native and having some problems to fetch the API data in the dropdown List. Basically I want to fetch the names from the API and display it in the drop down.\nFor a while I have added to countries. Below is my code for the same. I just want to fetch the name of the employee from the API.\n\n\n","excerpt":"flex: 1}\n     };\n    };\n    constructor(props) {\n     super(props);\n     this.state = {\n       loading: true,\n       dataSource:[]\n      };\n    }\n    componentDidMount(){\n    fetch(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to fetch API data in dropdown options in React Native expo dynamically"},{"tags":["javascript","jquery","vue.js","datatable","datatables"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":74163547,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1765386242,"creation_date":1666441611,"body":"I am new to Vue and I have been trying to use Vue with jquery datatables. I am working for a project in which I need to use jquery datatables.\nIn the following code snippets I tried to combine Vue with jquery datatables, but it doesn&#39;t work. The result is no creation of the datatable and no content. (I use Vue without npm)\nI would appreciate if someone could help me.\nHTML\n\nJavascript\n\n","excerpt":"Javascript\nconst { createApp } = Vue\n\nconst app = createApp({\n    data() {\n        return {\n            users:[]\n        }\n    },\n    mounted() {\n        $.ajax({\n            url: &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Using jquery Datatables with vue.js"},{"tags":["react-native"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":79843201,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79841217,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1765384289,"creation_date":1765384289,"body":"Full Flatlist code using basic functionality offered by phuocantd&#39;s answer:\n\n","excerpt":"useEffect, useRef, useState } from &#39;react&#39;;\nimport {\n  ActivityIndicator,\n  FlatList,\n  ListRenderItemInfo,\n  StyleSheet,\n  Text,\n  View,\n} from &#39;react-native&#39;;\n\nconst API_URL = &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Combine onMomentumScrollBegin and abortController in react native to avoid duplicate page fetches"},{"tags":["java","rest","post"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79842376,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1765375152,"creation_date":1765315797,"body":"I want to make an API caller with all CRUD methods using java\nI want to be able to get all the data with json then parse it and only get data with it&#39;s unique id\nThe thing that I can&#39;t figure out is how do I send data using an API. I get that I can use an id but what if I need to modify not one but 2 or more fields how do I do it then while Parsing a json?\nSo I have implemented the GET method but I can&#39;t think of how to implement the POST one\nHere is the code from my methods class where I have all the methods\nI&#39;m using Jackson to parse json and Java&#39;s Httpclient\n\nHere is how I get my data back\n\nThat&#39;s the output when I run it all\n\nI also have an error class\n\nas well as link class\n\nThat&#39;s what I have in main\n\nI started my programming classes a few months ago and that&#39;s my first project on my own\n","excerpt":"java.util.Collections;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\npublic class methods extends link{\n\n    private final ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();\n    private final String url = &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Httpclient in java send a POST request"},{"tags":["typescript","next.js","source-maps"],"question_score":6,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":79841082,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79837738,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1765205250,"creation_date":1765205250,"body":"I had the same issue, I fixed it with await just the params\n\n","excerpt":"IAlbums } from &quot;@/app/types&quot;;\n\nexport default async function AlbumPage({ params }: { params: Promise&lt;{id: string}&gt; }) {\n  const id = (await params).id\n  const res = await fetch(`https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Next.js source maps error &quot;Invalid source map. Only conformant source maps can be used to find the original code&quot;"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":77880574,"is_answered":false,"question_id":77877385,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1764342040,"creation_date":1706191568,"body":"Here&#39;s a setup using fetchQuery that might fit in your case:\n\nThe state has been oversimplified, along with a dummy JSON placeholder API call, just to make the point.\n","excerpt":"default function App() {\n  return (\n    &lt;QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}&gt;\n      &lt;Example /&gt;\n    &lt;/QueryClientProvider&gt;\n  );\n}\n\nfunction queryFn({ id = &#39;1&#39; }) {\n  const URL = &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How can I run dynamic query in TanStack Query?"},{"tags":["ios","swift","swiftui"],"question_score":4,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79795184,"item_type":"question","score":4,"last_activity_date":1764222026,"creation_date":1760985860,"body":"I have the code below which I&#39;m using in a SwiftUI view. When I compile this in Xcode 26.0.1 with iOS 26 I get this warning on the line that calls :\n\nMain actor-isolated conformance of &#39;Post&#39; to &#39;Decodable&#39; cannot be used in nonisolated context; this is an error in the Swift 6 language mode\n\nHow do I fix that? I want to use  rather than  because I&#39;ve found that using  in a class marked  from a SwiftUI view always runs on main thread, but I want the JSON decoding to happen on a background thread.\n\n","excerpt":"func fetchPost() {\n    guard let url = URL(string: &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/posts/1&quot;) else {\n      return\n    }\n\n    Task.detached { [weak self] in\n      guard let self else { return } &hellip; ","title":"In Swift how to resolve warning about main actor-isolated conformance cannot be used in nonisolated context?"},{"tags":["ios","swift","swiftui"],"question_score":4,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":79795760,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79795184,"item_type":"answer","score":3,"last_activity_date":1764222026,"creation_date":1761046201,"body":"Seems you are getting in a real mess with weak self, detached etc. Async/await requires thinking a bit differently about code so I think you need to start over from scratch with the following points in mind:\n\nWhen async is running it&#39;s essentially creating a lifetime (like an object) so you don&#39;t actually need a class anymore. So first you need to move your func outside of class. Class is for mutable state thus can&#39;t have any async instance funcs or it will corrupt the properties. This is one of the reasons Apple always stay start with struct. The way to have mutable state that is not corrupt by instance async funcs is actor but that is not the right tool for your problem, e.g. it&#39;s for implementing the model store for your whole app that saves, loads, syncs etc.\n\nWhat matters is where you define the async func, not where it is called from. Thus your async code that is inside view code, i.e. MainActor has zero chance of ever running on the background thread. Detached is not a valid solution to that because it is designed for when no UI update is required on completion, i.e. it would be valid for logging.\n\nAsync funcs usually always return a result.\n\n\nPutting this in practice looks something like:\ne.g.\n\nThen you can call it from  as follows:\n\nYou can improve on this by putting  in an  so then it can be replaced with a mock func for previews.\nTo guarantee  is not main actor you might have to turn off a new Xcode 26 setting which is just complicating the situation further.\n","excerpt":"static func fetchPost() async throws -&gt; Post {\n        let url = URL(string: &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/posts/1&quot;)! &hellip; ","title":"In Swift how to resolve warning about main actor-isolated conformance cannot be used in nonisolated context?"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs","fetch-api"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":77405103,"is_answered":false,"question_id":51204735,"item_type":"answer","score":-2,"last_activity_date":1764060428,"creation_date":1698866622,"body":"\n\n\n\n\n\n","excerpt":"const getapi = async () =&gt; {\n  try {\n    let res = await fetch(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/todos/2&quot;);\n    let fi = await res.json();\n    console.log(fi);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.log &hellip; ","title":"React js fetch API"},{"tags":["javascript","fetch-api"],"question_score":65,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":79826527,"is_answered":false,"question_id":45018338,"item_type":"answer","score":-1,"last_activity_date":1763733205,"creation_date":1763730565,"body":"You can kinda do it a hacky sort of way with storage...\n\n","excerpt":"(async function foo() { \n  const res = await fetch(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/posts/1&#39;);\n  let obj = await res.json();\n  let str = JSON.stringify(obj);\n  localStorage.setItem(&quot;mydata&quot;, str); &hellip; ","title":"Javascript Fetch API - How to save output to variable as an Object (not the Promise)"},{"tags":["reactjs","next.js","react-suspense"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79322031,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1763109471,"creation_date":1735752170,"body":"In React 19, I&#39;m trying to create a Server Function that works with a React client component (not a React Server Component) to perform an async fetch. If I put the async fetch directly in the client component, it fetches the data with no error, but when I move the async fetch into Server Function, I get an error as follows:\n\nIt feels like it should be unnecessary to add either  or  to React 19 code that includes the new use hook and Suspense.\nI have both ways of doing this in this GitHub repo: https://github.com/pkellner/react19-use-hook-server-function-issue\nThe problem code, that is the code that gets the error is this:\n\nand it&#39;s server action is:\n\nThe code that does not use a Server Function and works without error is this:\n\n","excerpt":"default App;\n\nand it&#39;s server action is:\n&#39;use server&#39;;\n\nexport async function fetchUsers() {\n  await new Promise((resolve) =&gt; setTimeout(resolve, 1000));\n  const res = await fetch(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; this:\n&quot;use client&quot;;\nimport { use, Suspense } from &quot;react&quot;;\n\nconst fetchUsers = async () =&gt; {\n  await new Promise((resolve) =&gt; setTimeout(resolve, 1000));\n  const res = await fetch(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Suspense with use hook and server action wanting useEffect"},{"tags":["json","rest","spring-mvc","curl","http-headers"],"question_score":3966,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":71027462,"is_answered":false,"question_id":7172784,"item_type":"answer","score":60,"last_activity_date":1763054327,"creation_date":1644283147,"body":"TL;DR:\nUse the holy trinity,  +  +  (or ):\n\nThis will cover necessary headers that were missing: no need to explicitly define the  and  headers.\nThe new curl way with --json\nEarly March 2022,  released a new command line parameter  with version 7.82.0. This allows for a shortcut to send through JSON and eliminating the need to define the  that you had missing and  headers as these are automatically assumed, hence reducing risk of mistakes:\n\nBut wait... there is more. Instead of defining the json parameter as a string to the  command line, use the nifty  CLI tool to define JSON as series of key value pairs and pipe the output through curl. Using  only to define your JSON, it works this way:\n\nLet&#39;s showcase this now with a similar  command of yours but without extra headers and using  +  for nice output:\n\nExample with a free API\nUsing a free mock API for demonstration:\n\nThe output has a pretty format thanks to :\n\n","excerpt":"8080/xx/xxx/xxxx | \\\njq\n\nExample with a free API\nUsing a free mock API for demonstration:\n&gt; jo title=&quot;Blog Post&quot; body=&quot;lorem ipsum&quot; userId=33 | \\\ncurl --json @- \\\n    -X POST \\\n    https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How do I POST JSON data with cURL?"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs","redux","react-redux"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79058542,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1762443376,"creation_date":1728198825,"body":"\nWhen I add the Users reducer in , in browser console reducers from redux logger are executing infinitely as shown here enter image description here\nI want to store the Users that I get from axios to the User reducer. And those users I want to access using state in  so that I can use as props . But the problem is redux logger infinitely logs state in my web browser console as shown in the image.\nHow to stop this?\nI tried many ways but did not find a proper solution.\n","excerpt":"dispatch({ type: &quot;USERS&quot;, payload: payload })\n});\n\nconst mapStateToProps= state =&gt; ({\n  ctr: state.TestReducer,\n  users: state.Users\n})  \n\nconst Dashboard = (props) =&gt; { \n  axios.get(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"React mapStateToProps state calling reducers infinitely"},{"tags":["c#",".net","razor","blazor","prerender"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79801713,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1761571501,"creation_date":1761561694,"body":"There are two pages in my app:\n (home) and . There is no problem rendering first page. But when I navigate to second page, there is flicker problem. I put 1000 ms sleep to better see the flickler. Whichever the page, this problem exists.\n\nOpen the app\n renders with no problem\nNavigate to , flicker problem\nOpen an incognito browser page\nPaste  link\nThere is no problem rendering \nNavigate to , flicker problem\n\nAlthough using a global  mode (in ) fixes the problem, my app uses no global render mode. I don&#39;t want this. I probably miss something in the component lifecycle. Can&#39;t figure out what. Anyone can help? Thank you for your time.\nBug produced github repo:\nhttps://github.com/kemgn/PersistenceBug\n:\n\n:\n\n:\n\n\n\n","excerpt":"result = await Http.GetFromJsonAsync&lt;Post[]&gt;(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/posts&quot;).ConfigureAwait(true);\n\n        return result ?? [];\n    }\n    protected override void OnDataLoaded(Post[]? &hellip; result = await Http.GetFromJsonAsync&lt;Comment[]&gt;(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/Comments&quot;).ConfigureAwait(true);\n\n        return result ?? &hellip; ","title":"Blazor auto render mode prerender flicker problem even though pages use persistence"},{"tags":["ajax","rxjs","rxjs-pipeable-operators"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":79793845,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79793841,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1760810827,"creation_date":1760803685,"body":"We can move the  inside the ajax Observable using pipe. Then use  alone for the outer pipe.\nThe  handles the failure and ensures the API stream continues.\n\nStackblitz Demo\n\nUsing Map:\nWe can also achieve using the below alternative code, same concept. We move the  inside the  so that the inner stream is error handled, not affecting the outer main stream.\n\nStackblitz Demo\n","excerpt":"&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/todosqqwrqewr/2&#39;, // error 404\n    &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/todos/3&#39;, // good URL, ajax request won&#39;t execute\n  ].map((url) =&gt;\n    ajax({\n      method &hellip; ://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/todosqqwrqewr/2&#39;, // error 404\n  &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/todos/3&#39;, // good URL, ajax request won&#39;t execute\n])\n  .pipe(\n    map((url: any) =&gt;\n      ajax({ &hellip; ","title":"How to prevent RxJS to stop pipeline execution on the first exception"},{"tags":["graphql"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":70332658,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1760002209,"creation_date":1639388845,"body":"Right now I&#39;m writing a React application.\nFor education purposes I&#39;d like to write own todo application, using some REST API service to fetch data (https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts for example)\nCan I write a couple of GraphQL queries to get data from this server knowing that their backend implementation does not support GraphQL queries?\nIn other words, can I use GraphQL on client, and write own backend (or request to one above) as a simple REST API service?\n","excerpt":"For education purposes I&#39;d like to write own todo application, using some REST API service to fetch data (https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/posts for example)\nCan I write a couple of GraphQL queries &hellip; ","title":"Can GraphQL work without server implementation?"},{"tags":["flutter","dart","asynchronous"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":75119702,"is_answered":false,"question_id":75119546,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1759402846,"creation_date":1673715488,"body":"Unawaited is used as a fire and forget method. So, you can&#39;t do anything with its response because it will continue in the code once the first  has been triggered.\nTo execute your , do the following:\n\nIf you only want to log the string, you can do it in your  function:\n\nBut if you want to do something else with your string, use another method and &quot;fire and forget&quot; that one:\n\nIn both my examples, the output will be the following:\n\n","excerpt":"following:\nunawaited(fetchApi(i));\n\nIf you only want to log the string, you can do it in your fetchApi function:\nFuture&lt;String&gt; fetchApi(int idNum) async {\n  final url = Uri.parse(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; Future&lt;void&gt; startSomething(int idNum) async {\n  final result = await fetchApi(idNum);\n  \n  print(result);\n}\n\nFuture&lt;String&gt; fetchApi(int idNum) async {\n  final url = Uri.parse(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to properly use unawaited in dart?"},{"tags":["datatables"],"question_score":-1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":79780207,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79779364,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1759332417,"creation_date":1759330579,"body":"Here is a minimal runnable example, using data provided from an AJAX source (a test URL service, which provides JSON data):\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is based on this official example, but adapted for AJAX-sourced data, as shown in various examples, such as this one.\nThis may give you some ideas for your own solution. The main point is: it uses DataTables&#39; built-in support for Ajax, which simplifies the overall code.\n\nWarning: In my MRE, I use  because that matches the structure of the JSON provided by the URL I am using. But your JSON may have a different overall structure (at the outermost level of the JSON) - and therefore you may need to change this option to match your JSON.\nSee also When using Ajax with jQuery DataTables, how do I determine what to do with the data returned?\n","excerpt":"&lt;script&gt;\n    $(document).ready(function() {\n\n\n      var table = $(&#39;#example&#39;).DataTable({\n        orderCellsTop: true,\n        ajax: {\n          method: &quot;GET&quot;,\n          url: &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"DataTables how to update select filters based on other select filter but json as source"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs","next.js"],"question_score":11,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":4,"is_answered":true,"question_id":64052148,"item_type":"question","score":11,"last_activity_date":1759218544,"creation_date":1600971367,"body":"I fetch a list of posts in index js like this :\n\nAnd when user clicks on any link it goes to post page which is :\n\nThe problem is when I click back the scroll position resets to top and it fetches all posts .\nI included  in Link but it doesn&#39;t work .\nHow can I prevent scroll resetting when user clicks back from the post page ?\n","excerpt":"h1&gt;\n                        &lt;/a&gt;\n                    &lt;/Link&gt;\n                );\n            })}\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n    );\n};\n\nexport async function getStaticProps() {\n    const url = `https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; { post }) {\n    return (\n            &lt;h1&gt;{post.id}&lt;/h1&gt;\n    );\n}\n\nexport async function getServerSideProps({ query }) {\n    const { id } = query;\n    const res = await Axios.get(`https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to change scroll behavior while going back in next js?"},{"tags":["javascript","jquery","ajax"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":73319473,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1759055782,"creation_date":1660215354,"body":"I&#39;m learning jQuery and using fake data for Ajax requests. Here is simple HTML:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEverything was working yesterday. But today, when I run the script, it builds divs with data and then everything disappears (without reloading).\n","excerpt":"Here is simple HTML:\n\n\n$(function() {\n  $(&#39;.tasks__form&#39;).on(&#39;submit&#39;, function() {\n    let id = $(&#39;.tasks__input&#39;).val();\n    $.ajax({\n      type: &#39;GET&#39;,\n      url: &#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"Data disapearing after AJAX request"},{"tags":["javascript","vuejs2","emit"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":54972782,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1758963271,"creation_date":1551641077,"body":"I&#39;m having an issue in getting  to work to send up data to the parent. What I wish to do is on click of the submit button take the data from the inputs and then send the results up to the parent. I&#39;m using a prototype  block just to test the flow.\n\nTypeError: Cannot read property &#39;$emit&#39; of undefined\nat eval (SearchBar.vue?e266:42)\n\n\n","excerpt":"todate: this.todate,\n            namesearch: this.namesearch,\n            titlesearch: this.titlesearch,\n            descsearch: this.descsearch\n        }\n            axios.get(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"VueJS $emit not working to push data to parent"},{"tags":["node.js","web-scraping","puppeteer"],"question_score":17,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":78381785,"is_answered":false,"question_id":48511357,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1758295635,"creation_date":1714006066,"body":"Puppeteer is a browser automation tool, so if you&#39;re just making a request to get a raw JSON document, there&#39;s nothing to automate. Prefer using Node&#39;s native , possibly with a browser user agent or cookies/headers if you&#39;re running into a server block:\n\nThis is faster and simpler than Puppeteer and has no dependency or install step.\nIf you really need Puppeteer for some reason, possibly to bypass a block or include live credentials from a site, you can do it as follows:\n\nThis is better practice than existing answers: it closes the browser if an error is thrown, uses the response returned by  to avoid having to use  or , and uses  which is the fastest navigation wait condition ( will unnecessarily wait for 500ms after fetching the document).\nSpeed comparison. Fetch:\n\nPuppeteer:\n\nAnother trick to keep in mind about fetch: it works in the browser, which can be useful for cases when you need to hit a protected API with same origin credentials from the page, imitating a call from the client. In this case, you can run  from an  block.\n","excerpt":"Prefer using Node&#39;s native fetch, possibly with a browser user agent or cookies/headers if you&#39;re running into a server block:\nconst url = &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span>/users&quot;;\n\nfetch(url)\n  .then &hellip; Puppeteer for some reason, possibly to bypass a block or include live credentials from a site, you can do it as follows:\nconst puppeteer = require(&quot;puppeteer&quot;); // ^22.6.0\n\nconst url = &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to scrape JSON from puppeteer?"},{"tags":["javascript","vue.js","vuejs2","axios","vue-router"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":55739064,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1757454408,"creation_date":1555560978,"body":"I am doing a project with Vuejs and I need to the following:\n\nUse an API &amp; fetch a list of users (just the names of the users) in the home page.\n\nCreate a custom search filter to find users by name.\n\nWhen clicking on a user&#39;s name, I need to redirect to another component &amp; output that user&#39;s details in that component (only the details of the user that I clicked).\n\n\nI have accomplished the first two tasks. However, I have no idea how doing the other third task. I was reading the documentation for vue-router, but I am not able to figure it out.\nI used axios to fetch the list of users &amp; jsonplaceholder.\nUser List Component:\n\nThe User list component&#39;s name is \nI need to ouput the user detail in this component called \n\nScreenshot user list &amp; custom search filter\n\n\n","excerpt":"filteredUsers() {\n      return this.users.filter(user =&gt; {\n        return user.name.match(this.searchUsers)\n      })\n    }\n  },\n  // life cycle hook - calls axios\n  created(){\n    axios.get(&#39;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to click on a user &amp; show the user details in another component/view with Vuejs router?"},{"tags":["reactjs","next.js","react-query","react-suspense"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":79286229,"item_type":"question","score":3,"last_activity_date":1756822849,"creation_date":1734388341,"body":"I have a reproduction for this issue here.\nI&#39;m playing around with NextJS app router, and Suspense.\nI have two implementations of a simple client component that fetches data with React Query. One uses  the other uses a regular query.\n\n\nIn my App router page, I can render  either of these components:\n\nor\n\nIntuitively,  what I&#39;m expecting here is that server render will render application in it&#39;s loading state, stream that to the client, and then the client takes over and makes the API call.\nHowever, what I actually observe, is that in the case of using the suspense query, actually NextJS applies static rendering to  component. That is, in a production build, it returns prerendered HTML, never making the 10 second wait.\nIt&#39;s important to observe both the behaviour of the dev server, as well as the production build.\n\n\n\n\nDev Server\nProduction Build\n\n\n\n\nTodosRq\nWe don&#39;t see the suspense boundary. We wait 10 seconds till content appears. Content does not appear in the root document.\nWe don&#39;t see the suspense boundary. We wait 10 seconds till content appears. Content does not appear in the root document.\n\n\nTodosRqSuspense\nWe see the suspense boundary. We wait 10 seconds till content appears. Content appears in the root document. (The dev server appears to do something funny where it can modify the response body of the network request)\nWe get the content immediately. Content is in the root document.\n\n\n\nWhat am I missing here?\nHere&#39;s the relevant parts of the documentation and how I understand it:\nStatic vs Dynamic rendering - for server components default behaviour is that all content will statically rendered (that is, rendered at build time), even if it involves data fetching, unless it fits into one of the exceptions, such as using the  or  methods.\nClient components - Client components are pre-rendered on the server, (first render on the server), and but then when they hit the client then the work is done on the client.\nSuspense - Allows the &#39;first render&#39; to show all the loading skeletons etc, and then if using RSCs then they&#39;ll stream in, and, this is where I am having some misunderstanding, I would have thought that client components would still do their data fetching client side, and then display when they are complete.\nWhat NextJS recommends - NextJS recommend that you do your data fetching in server components, just to be clear. However - within the context of some kind of migration, it makes sense that we might keep some things as client components. In any case, I&#39;m trying to understand the nuance here.\nnb. if we add  to our client component, then this behaviour does not occur and behaves inline with how I&#39;ve intuited.\n","excerpt":"useQuery&lt;Array&lt;{id: number, title: string}&gt;&gt;({ queryKey: [&#39;todos&#39;], queryFn: async () =&gt; {\n\n        await new Promise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(res, 10000));\n        const res = await  fetch(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; useSuspenseQuery&lt;Array&lt;{id: number, title: string}&gt;&gt;({ queryKey: [&#39;todos&#39;], queryFn: async () =&gt; {\n\n        await new Promise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(res, 10000));\n        const res = await  fetch(&quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"NextJS app router: Client component with data fetching, inside a suspense boundary gets statically rendered"},{"tags":["javascript","html","ajax","axios"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":70793445,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1756564917,"creation_date":1642713116,"body":"I need to write an ID (from 1 to 10) and to be displayed on a table but I don&#39;t know how to bring the ID I wrote to the print, how do I display ONLY the data from certain ID of the JSON file?\n\n\n","excerpt":"&lt;th&gt;ID&lt;/th&gt;\n            &lt;th&gt;Title&lt;/th&gt;\n            &lt;th&gt;Completed&lt;/th&gt;\n        &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;/thead&gt;\n    &lt;tbody id=&quot;tabla&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;\n\nfunction ajax() {\n    const url = &quot;https://<span class=\"highlight\">jsonplaceholder.typicode.com</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to make the text/id I give can be brought from the URL I am requesting"},{"tags":["javascript","vuejs3"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79748996,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1756379891,"creation_date":1756379891,"body":"I am getting a api respose which contains string. basically it contains code for a composable that I have to run in my FormBuilder. I have given a example of what I am trying 